notes=[
'**Statement 009-N1 — manuscript claims.** The page begins an explanation because of the property’s importance, leaving the introductory sentence unfinished at “d’autres”. Cancelled At DC1 and two corollaries are followed by a cancelled, unfinished At DC2 (“Alors”). The live “On voudra la” introduces Propriété1, an equivalence between compatibility of refinements and compatibility of their L-indexed restrictions. The reference line asserts one direction with a two-shaft, rounded-return mark; the separate attempted proof beginning “Montrons…” is cancelled. The later axiom relates this to the old At12 and is headed At DD1. No equivalence or full axiom is proved by the transcription (Grothendieck, 1986, scan9).',
'**Statement 009-N2 — limited NB-tail check.** R2 checked the final contradiction under explicit assumptions that Z is a nonempty stratum, Z≪L and Z∥L. Disjointness gives compatibility and Z∩L=∅. At4, applied using Z itself among its strata, supplies U∈L-tilde with Z≪U. Compatibility descends from L to U; At5 for compatible strata then gives Z≤U≤L, hence Z∩L=Z, contrary to nonemptiness. M rechecked this argument. M’s earlier provisional shortcut applied At5 directly to Z,L, although L need not be a stratum; the corrected argument includes At4 and U. The preceding step from common refinements to Z≪X∩Y and the new Z/Z′ line-attribution doubt remain unproved. This is not an independent proof of the complete upper marginal argument.',
'**Statement 009-N3 — conditional hereditary-compatibility check.** R2 checked that if A≤F′ and B≤G′ and the compatible parent figures admit a common upper figure H, then H is also an upper figure for A and B. M rechecked that order argument. Its application to F′_L and G′_L is conditional on their being subfigures of their parents; that restriction definition is not established on this page. Neither the displayed equivalence nor its converse is thereby certified.',
'**Statement 009-N4 — literal cancelled Cor1 under a stated local interpretation.** R2 supplied the two-element Boolean figure poset {∅,{a}}, refinement taken as inclusion and all figures compatible. With F=C=G=C′=∅ and F′=G′={a}, the written F∥C|G, F≪F and C′≪G premises hold but the F′∥G′ conclusion fails. M rechecked those truth values. This refutes the universally quantified implication under that explicit interpretation, irrespective of the C/G alternative; the model was not certified against every atelier axiom. Refined scope **009-N4R**: the written premises alone do not constrain the two primed conclusion variables sufficiently in this interpretation. No repaired theorem or replacement manuscript letter is asserted.',
'**Statement 009-N5 — local computation for live Corollaire2.** R3 computed with finite sets, disjointness as ∥ and inclusion as ≪: F=F′={0}, G=C′={1}, G′={0}. All three literal antecedents are true and F′∥G′ is false. The certificate is retained in readers/R3/scan009_math_check.json. M inspected and rechecked the assignment and result without claiming a second computation. This establishes the substantive effect of the C′/G′ mismatch under that interpretation; it was not certified as a model of all atelier axioms and does not validate an editorial emendation.',
'**Statement 009-N6 — author’s counterexample claim, not independently certified.** The lower margin calls the criterion false “dans le cas simplicial” and gives a quadrilateral/oval drawing. Its later note claims a counterexample to At∥ and “a fortiori” to At11. The local restriction notation and identities of the geometric pieces are insufficiently specified in these pages for an independent certification in this run. The four-stroke relation is reproduced literally without asserting a standardized negation meaning. The final disjointness equivalence remains a manuscript claim, as do the references to old At12 and the outside GF VI pages; none of those outside pages was consulted.',
'**Reading decisions and literal slips.** The first cancelled Cor1 declares F,C, has F∥C|G, F≪F without a prime and C′≪G. Three additional premises—cancelled Cor2, live Corollaire2 and Plus gén.—read C′≪G against both supplied witnesses’ G′. R2’s original G′ readings and its separate neutral supplement are both preserved; the latter agrees with the final C′. The conclusions still use G′. The live axiom defines K but writes L in its restrictions. DD and the oblique ancien are resolved from letter contours, with ancien’s physical placement preserved and its grammatical attachment left open. The old Sup equation is uncertain as a whole. The lower NB favors l’inverse over l’énoncé but remains doubtful, as do its tiny terminal marks and the older est. The small separator and three drawing crosses are reproduced geometrically rather than assigned a semantic identity.',
'**Scope and documentary details.** Manuscript page8 is written at the top; this page has no new date or title sheet. All34 C doubts were audited. The upper slanted NB is treated as globally cancelled, with its local earlier changes separately marked. At DC2’s underline excludes the first Y′; the lower frame remains open. The live reference is not struck together with the proof attempt beneath it. H’s same-span emphasis and its ordinary between glyph are not counted merely for macro syntax; exact span, placement and the locally retraced relation are recorded separately. There is no S correction on this scan.'
]
